WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.370
London, January 1684.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:12.790
The River Thames has frozen so hard that there are streets of stalls on the ice, meat roasting, and coaches driving across: a frost fair.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.870
We know, because John Evelyn wrote it in his diary at the time.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.710
For two centuries, it froze like this again and again.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.530
The last fair was in 1814.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.670
Since then: never.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.550
Why did the River Thames freeze and then stop freezing?

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:35.790
In this mission, you'll read Evelyn's diary and work out what one source can and can't prove.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.670
You'll find out what makes a river freeze, and put your explanation to the test.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.010
Your mission: explain why the Thames froze, and why it stopped.
